==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Madam King''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Madam the Savannah''' when obtained from the [[Bride Awakens!]] (may be dropped on the first stage but guaranteed on the second stage) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Madam Bride is basically just a very expensive meatshield. Her high cost and long recharge time makes her quite difficult to use despite her high health. [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]] stall better than her in generally all other situations. [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Sumo Cat]] completely outclasses her, with better health, spammability and cost-efficiency.

Her main use lies in the [[Cat Combo|Combos]] [[Seasons of Love (Combo)|Seasons of Love]], [[Lion King (Combo)|Lion King]] and [[Three Kings (Combo)|Three Kings]] as she is in all of them and if you have the required cats, they can all be active at once, granting a noticeable benefit for units needing them, such as [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cats]] in [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|Realm of Carnage]] against [[Hannya]] and [[Bore]].

==='''True Form'''===
Madam the Savannah finally has worthwhile stats! Only barely though, but she can be used, as long as she is aided by [[Catseye]]s or Cat Combos, where she can find use by stalling lone boss enemies like [[Mystic Mask Yulala]]. However, these do not stop other simple meatshields from simply outclassing her, plus [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] and [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Dogumaru]] do better at stalling the said boss enemy, so it ends up changing little and isn't of any priority, given it also does not grant access to new combos.

